              "text": "**Gary Brooker**, the lead vocalist and pianist for the English rock band **Procol Harum**, was the first to sing \"A Whiter Shade of Pale\". \n\nThe song was released as the band's debut single on **May 12, 1967**, and quickly became a massive global hit and an anthem of the \"Summer of Love\". \n\nThe music was written by Gary Brooker and the band's organist Matthew Fisher (influenced heavily by Johann Sebastian Bach), while the surreal lyrics were written by Keith Reid. Since its 1967 release, the song has been covered more than 1,000 times by other artists, but Brooker's soulful, original performance remains the most famous.",
